I removed Antigravity (agy) support for 0.10.0. A few completion conditions are still open because they touch protected settings that I'm not allowed to change. The 11 unit test files affected by the change pass (249 tests). The required checks (`typecheck`, `lint:ts`, `test:unit`, `lint:md` and the others) are run by the parent runner afterwards.

**Before you build:** this repository's own `.specdojo/agent-members.yaml` still has 11 agy members (all `disabled: true`). With this change they cause an error when the member list is loaded, so a build that includes this change can't read that file until those members are deleted. They need to go before you build or ship.

**What changed (53 files)**
- **Code:** deleted the agy provider code (`src/shared/antigravity-block.ts`, `src/exec/antigravity-session.ts`) and the 0.9.2 code that stopped agy from launching. Removed `antigravity` from the provider type, the extra-directory arguments, `orchestrator launch`, `init` and `devcontainer scaffold`, plus the internal `agent launch` command.
- **New error:** loading `agent-members.yaml` now fails for any member with `provider: antigravity`, even if it is disabled. The message gives the reason and the fix. Two new tests in `tests/src/shared/specdojo-config.test.ts` cover the disabled and enabled cases.
- **`--global`:** it only ever applied to agy's user settings. I removed the merge code but kept the option, which now errors before anything is written. Whether to drop the option entirely is in the handoff.
- **Templates:** deleted `templates/antigravity/`. Removed the agy members, aliases and `providers.antigravity` from the `init` templates, and the `~/.config/antigravity` line from `templates/devcontainer/post-create.sh`.
- **Tools:** took `templates/antigravity/orchestrator.md` off the orchestrator sync list (`npm run lint:orchestrator-sync` passes with 9 targets). Removed agy from `update-agent-clis.mjs` and `verify-multi-repo-agent-write.sh`.
- **Tests:** deleted 3 agy-only test files and the agy cases in the others.
- **Docs:** removed agy from 9 guides and references under `docs/ja/specdojo` and from `README.md`. `command-reference` and `README.md` keep one paragraph on why it was removed and how to migrate. The 0.3.0 migration guide and `CHANGELOG.md` are unchanged.
- **Ticket:** filled in the work table and the results section: the full list of what was removed and what was kept (with reasons), the proposed protected changes, and the CHANGELOG draft in 5.1 (section: removal, with migration steps).

**Not done, and why**
- **`.agents/rules/*.md`:** the 6 agy wrappers are under a protected path, so I couldn't delete them. The proposal to delete them is in the ticket and handoff.
- **Schemas:** `antigravity` stays allowed in `agent-members.schema.yaml` and `exec-defaults.schema.yaml`. This repo's protected settings still use it, so removing it now would fail `npm run validate:schema`. The new error runs before schema validation, so agy members are rejected anyway.
- **Out of scope:** this repo's `.devcontainer/` and `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and the product design docs under `docs/ja/product/040-system-design/`.
- **Work table:** row 5 ("pass the checks") is left `open` because only the runner can confirm it.
- **Deletions already staged:** my first deletion used `git rm`, so those deletions are already staged. Unstaging needs approval, so I left them; the file contents are the same either way.

Checks I ran myself: `npm run validate:history-links` and markdownlint on the changed docs both pass. I ran Prettier on the changed files.

